WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:07.062
Maggie gasped.

2
00:00:07.082 --> 00:00:18.106
"Oh my gosh," she said.

3
00:00:18.126 --> 00:00:19.947
"You're right, Henry!

4
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:26.610
I forgot that Nathan and Nora were only wearing bathing suits when they stopped at the lemonade stand."

5
00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.911
"Me too," Cole said.

6
00:00:28.931 --> 00:00:31.872
"But I remember now," Maggie went on.

7
00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:36.275
"Nathan dripped all over my shoes while I was talking to him."

8
00:00:36.295 --> 00:00:40.779
"Sorry about that," Nathan said sheepishly.

9
00:00:40.799 --> 00:00:43.641
"We forgot to bring towels to the pool.

10
00:00:44.222 --> 00:00:45.423
Good thing it was a hot day."

11
00:00:45.443 --> 00:00:50.106
"That's why you had to borrow money to buy lemonade, right?"

12
00:00:50.407 --> 00:00:51.087
Henry said.

13
00:00:51.988 --> 00:00:52.788
Nathan nodded.

14
00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:56.832
"We didn't bring anything with us to the pool," he said.

15
00:00:56.852 --> 00:00:58.953
"But Mrs.

16
00:00:59.014 --> 00:01:01.816
Martin let us borrow enough money to buy two cups of lemonade."

17
00:01:03.032 --> 00:01:05.494
"So you guys really didn't take my money?"

18
00:01:05.854 --> 00:01:06.615
Maggie asked.

19
00:01:07.495 --> 00:01:09.176
She sounded kind of disappointed.

20
00:01:09.196 --> 00:01:14.120
"You said yourself there was lots of money in your cashbox," Cole said to Maggie.

21
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.142
"Was there too much for Nora to hide in her hands?"

22
00:01:17.162 --> 00:01:20.224
"Definitely," Maggie said.

23
00:01:20.244 --> 00:01:24.527
"There were a bunch of dollar bills and lots of change too.

24
00:01:25.568 --> 00:01:27.989
Way too much for anyone to hide in their hands."

25
00:01:28.009 --> 00:01:31.432
"I guess that proves it," Henry said.

26
00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.341
"Nathan and Nora couldn't have done it."

27
00:01:34.361 --> 00:01:36.761
"Yeah," Cole added.

28
00:01:36.781 --> 00:01:39.002
"Sorry we accused you guys."

29
00:01:39.022 --> 00:01:42.743
"It's all right," Nathan said with a smile.

30
00:01:42.763 --> 00:01:47.364
"Cool," Henry said, glad that Nathan wasn't angry.

31
00:01:47.384 --> 00:01:51.985
"Sorry I took the extra lemonade, Maggie," Nora said.

32
00:01:52.005 --> 00:01:55.146
"I was just really thirsty after swimming."

33
00:01:55.166 --> 00:01:58.647
"That's okay," Maggie told the younger girl.

34
00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:02.468
"But please remember to ask next time, okay?"

35
00:02:03.549 --> 00:02:04.350
"I promise!"

36
00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:05.231
Nora said.

37
00:02:05.251 --> 00:02:07.152
"So now what?"

38
00:02:07.533 --> 00:02:08.253
Cole shrugged.

39
00:02:09.274 --> 00:02:10.795
"Nora and Nathan didn't take the money.

40
00:02:11.716 --> 00:02:13.578
Those two teenage girls didn't do it either.

41
00:02:14.438 --> 00:02:15.219
Neither did Ryan."

42
00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.001
Cole stared at Henry and Maggie.

43
00:02:18.882 --> 00:02:19.783
They stared back.

44
00:02:20.763 --> 00:02:23.546
Henry knew they were all thinking the same thing.

45
00:02:23.566 --> 00:02:25.647
"So who did it?"

46
00:02:26.068 --> 00:02:26.648
he asked.

47
00:02:27.589 --> 00:02:29.070
"We're all out of suspects."

48
00:02:30.351 --> 00:02:32.109
"No, we're not," Maggie said.

49
00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:33.650
"What about Mrs.

50
00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.752
Martin? She was hanging around when the cash went missing."

51
00:02:37.772 --> 00:02:39.413
"Mrs. Martin?"

52
00:02:39.714 --> 00:02:40.254
Cole said.

53
00:02:40.274 --> 00:02:42.776
"We already talked about that, remember?

54
00:02:43.756 --> 00:02:44.837
She couldn't be the thief.

55
00:02:45.618 --> 00:02:46.698
She's a police officer."

56
00:02:47.539 --> 00:02:49.500
Nora wasn't paying attention anymore.

57
00:02:50.521 --> 00:02:54.464
She and her friend were already back to arguing about who was a better princess.

58
00:02:55.905 --> 00:02:58.366
But Nathan was still listening to Henry and his friends.

59
00:02:58.386 --> 00:03:02.069
"Not right now she isn't," he pointed out.

60
00:03:02.089 --> 00:03:05.571
"Mrs. Martin took time off from the police force.

61
00:03:06.912 --> 00:03:09.234
She's going back to work when Marty gets a little older."

62
00:03:09.254 --> 00:03:11.756
"I forgot about that!"

63
00:03:12.036 --> 00:03:12.976
Maggie exclaimed.

64
00:03:12.996 --> 00:03:17.680
"Me too, but that's not the point," Henry said.

65
00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:21.422
"Mrs. Martin is an honest person and a mother.

66
00:03:22.323 --> 00:03:25.745
She wouldn't steal money, especially not from a kid."

67
00:03:25.765 --> 00:03:28.247
"How do we know that for sure?"

68
00:03:28.587 --> 00:03:29.248
Maggie said.

69
00:03:30.028 --> 00:03:33.130
"What if she's short of cash right now since she isn't working?"

70
00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:36.112
"Don't be silly," Cole said.

71
00:03:36.132 --> 00:03:38.513
"Mr. Martin still has a job.

72
00:03:39.254 --> 00:03:40.674
He's a teacher at the college."

73
00:03:40.694 --> 00:03:43.336
"But what if he doesn't make enough money?"

74
00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:44.297
Maggie said.

75
00:03:44.317 --> 00:03:49.320
"They used to have two salaries to pay the bills, and now they only have one.

76
00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.702
Plus they have a kid who's growing and needs stuff all the time."

77
00:03:54.703 --> 00:03:56.344
She stared around at all of them.

78
00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.062
"Maybe they barely have enough to get by, and she's desperate.

79
00:04:01.843 --> 00:04:04.525
Desperate enough to steal any money she can find!"

80
00:04:05.485 --> 00:04:06.386
Henry sighed.

81
00:04:06.406 --> 00:04:11.529
"That sounds more like something from a movie than real life, Maggie."

82
00:04:11.549 --> 00:04:14.571
"Besides I don't think Mrs.

83
00:04:14.611 --> 00:04:16.993
Martin is that desperate," Nathan added.

84
00:04:17.013 --> 00:04:19.975
"She bought lemonade for Nora and me, remember?

85
00:04:21.816 --> 00:04:24.738
Plus she bought two cups for herself and one for Marty."

86
00:04:26.419 --> 00:04:30.443
"Marty?" Nora looked up suddenly at the sound of Marty's name.

87
00:04:30.463 --> 00:04:35.488
"Yuck! I don't like Marty Martin one bit!"

88
00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:39.733
Maggie, Nathan, and Cole didn't even look over at her.

89
00:04:40.654 --> 00:04:41.555
But Henry did.

90
00:04:41.575 --> 00:04:44.177
"What do you mean, Nora?"

91
00:04:44.518 --> 00:04:45.098
he asked.

92
00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:47.881
"Why don't you like Marty Martin?"

93
00:04:48.882 --> 00:04:50.044
Nora scowled.

94
00:04:50.988 --> 00:04:56.891
"When my mom babysits him at our house, he's always grabbing my stuff and saying it's his," she

95
00:04:56.971 --> 00:05:02.875
complained. "He even tried to take my microphone so I couldn't play rock star anymore!"

96
00:05:02.895 --> 00:05:04.696
"No way!"

97
00:05:05.196 --> 00:05:06.156
her friend cried.

98
00:05:06.176 --> 00:05:07.937
"That's mean!"

99
00:05:08.838 --> 00:05:10.979
Henry hardly heard the other little girl.

100
00:05:10.999 --> 00:05:13.040
"That's it!"

101
00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:14.041
he cried.

102
00:05:14.061 --> 00:05:15.421
"That's what?"

103
00:05:15.741 --> 00:05:16.482
Cole asked.

104
00:05:16.502 --> 00:05:20.084
"It was that little kid, Marty Martin!"

105
00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:21.500
Henry exclaimed.

106
00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.641
"He's our thief!"

107
00:05:24.602 --> 00:05:25.902
"Are you crazy?"

108
00:05:26.222 --> 00:05:26.863
Maggie said.

109
00:05:26.883 --> 00:05:29.304
"How could Marty be the thief?"

110
00:05:29.324 --> 00:05:32.245
"Yeah," Cole agreed.

111
00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:34.446
"Marty is only three years old.

112
00:05:35.386 --> 00:05:36.987
He doesn't even know what money is yet!"

113
00:05:37.867 --> 00:05:38.987
"It doesn't matter."

114
00:05:39.328 --> 00:05:42.169
Henry grinned, certain that he was right this time.

115
00:05:42.189 --> 00:05:48.031
"He probably doesn't know what a microphone is either, and Nora just said he took hers.

116
00:05:49.031 --> 00:05:49.912
Now come on, guys.

117
00:05:50.902 --> 00:05:52.637
Let's go get Maggie's money back!"
